.TH _CJSON_GET 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
_cjson_get \- path-navigation back-end (prefer cjson_get macro)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cjson.h>

cjson _cjson_get(cjson root, const char *path);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Navigates from root through a dot-separated path and returns the node at
the destination.  Path components starting with '#' followed by decimal
digits address array elements when the current node is CJSON_LIST;
otherwise they are treated as literal object keys.

Escape sequences in path components:
  \e.   -> literal '.' in the key (not a path separator)
  \e\e   -> literal '\e' in the key
A '\e' before any other character is left unchanged.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Non-owning node reference, or NULL if any component is missing or the
type at that step is incompatible.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cjson_get (macro) (3),
.BR _cjson_set_typed (3)
